accTitle: Continuous replication prepares the standby for failover
accDescr: During normal operation the primary serves requests and replicates continuously to a standby, which RDS promotes after failure.
subgraph H["Healthy operation"]
 U["Application reads and writes"] --> P[("Oracle primary in AZ A")]
 P -->|"continuous synchronous replication"| S[("Standby in AZ B")]
end
F["Primary or AZ failure"] --> R["RDS promotes existing standby"]
S --> R
R --> D["Existing endpoint DNS maps to new writer"]
D --> C["Application reconnects and resumes"]
